From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: Linux apps ask for the location

Linux apps get the location through GeoClue: Flatpak apps through
xdg-desktop-portal's Location portal, which asks once per app through the
Access portal's backend (NickelAccessAsk, 0060), and apps outside a
sandbox from GeoClue directly. ChromeOS's location switch in Privacy
controls decides for all of them, as for its own apps:

- NickelAccessAsk: the Location portal's question ("find-location-symbolic")
  in ChromeOS's words, with the location icon; with the switch off (or on
  for ChromeOS only), the notice that location access is off, with the
  button to Privacy controls, answered "off" (not remembered). The camera's
  and the location's dialogs come from one table.
- NickelLocationAllowed() -> (b): whether the switch lets apps use the
  location. nickel-appd's GeoClue agent asks while GeoClue runs and gives
  GeoClue no accuracy at all while it is off, which stops every app.

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ash/dbus/vm/BUILD.gn b/chrome/browser/ash/dbus/vm/BUILD.gn
index e87b1f1219d4a..36d731d9ddbea 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ash/dbus/vm/BUILD.gn
+++ b/chrome/browser/ash/dbus/vm/BUILD.gn
@@ -87,6 +87,7 @@ static_library("vm") {
     "//components/session_manager/core",
     "//components/tabs:public",
     "//components/user_manager",
+    "//components/vector_icons",
     "//media/capture:capture_lib",
     "//ui/base/clipboard",
     "//ui/base/clipboard:file_info",
